{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789479793,"nonce":"jotEB14gOVu9AKjgn9+BBjXsA8A=","title":"The typed array and SIMD classes are not roots","message":"byte_array_class, int32_array_class, float32_array_class, float64_array_class, simd_class, simd4f_class and simd4i_class are made at VM::new like the other core classes but are not among the class roots the collector gathers (the 20 in collect_garbage's step 3), and are not written back after a moving collection either. They survive natively only through the module variables core_class_value pre-populates, so a collection before the first module loads, or in a program with none, frees them; caribou hit it as a Wren cycle before its first module (issue 16d8592 there: a class's method table read from freed memory).","files":null}]}